  "pathwayDescription": "The Vietnam Energy Outlook Report is a governmental publication, developed by the Electricity and Renewable Energy Authority (EREA) in collaboration with external partners, that provides multiple potential pathways for Vietnam's energy sector. Its Net Zero+ scenario is a more ambitious extension of the Net Zero pathway, tightening the carbon limit to achieve 0 Mt of energy sector emissions by 2050. It tests how far Vietnam can push tech deployment and system transformation, and it investigates which technology areas applied to which sectors would be most cost-efficient to further reduce emissions. Compared to the Net Zero pathway, Net Zero+ adds faster and greater renewable build-out, as well as carbon capture and direct air capture, with 10 Mt being captured in 2050. Additionally, Net Zero+ introduces nuclear power build-out starting in 2040 that reaches 28 GW by 2050, as well as greater amounts of hydrogen produced for the decarbonization of industry and transport (573 PJ produced compared to 334 PJ in the Net Zero scenario). Fuel cost savings as compared to Baseline are greater in the Net Zero+ scenario than in the Net Zero pathway. Net Zero+ has the highest capital expenditure requirements of any of the EREA pathways. This scenario offers the greatest reduction in air pollution costs (i.e., the costs associated with the impact of air pollution on human health): 34% less than Baseline.",
